attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 16, `osmY` to `lgoD`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 17% of calls {S1}. The model names 18 to 100% of them, fewest at column 9, `yjjQ`, 18% {S1}.

@variable **A short fork follows the spine**, columns 17 and 18, `lgoR` and `lgoT`, shell, carried by 86 and 73% {S2.c17, S2.c18}. Then a branch of 11 shell families runs through columns 20 to 30, [[4-hydroxyphenylacetate catabolism]], carried by 28 to 33% {S4.b20, Q}. The `fim` genes, columns 46 to 54, are [[type 1 fimbria]], carried by 59 to 74% {S4.c46-54, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 89 against 81%, and hesitates less there, 0.40 against 0.86 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 41, `uxuR`, a fork column, 1.31 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in variable and fork columns.** Columns 57 to 71, `YthB` to `lptF`, are carried by 4 to 47% {S4.c57-71}. The last column is `ahr`, in 31% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 83% of genes**, 0.76 bits on average, perplexity 2.2 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.21 against 0.37 bits, and names fewer genes, 71% against 94% {C}.

